    basic: "If your hand is weak but contains a lone 10, try to play it on your partner's lead early to guarantee it isn't 'filtered' out by the opponents.",
    intermediate: "The Throw-in: Use the 'no trumps, no count' rule strategically to reset a hand where the opponents likely have all the power cards.",
    advanced: "Defensive Pitching: If you have a poor hand, pitch a suit where you hold a 'bobby' (low card) in hopes that your partner can dominate with the High or Jack.",
    tips: [
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "Count the pips constantly. Since A, K, Q, J, 10 represent all the value, knowing who has captured a 10 is the key to predicting the 'Game' point.",
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "Remember that 'Low' is for the card dealt. Even if you lose your 2 of trumps on the first trick, your side still pegs the point at the end.",
